    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "TOR 38, BOS 29",
        "text": "Toronto went 10-of-18 from three, tying a franchise record for a quarter, and Ja'Kobe Walter scored all 12 of his first-quarter points on threes. Fifteen of the Raptors' first 19 shots were threes."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "TOR 61, BOS 54",
        "text": "Immanuel Quickley's three made it 46–32 with 9:40 left, and Toronto led 59–37 with 5:24 to go. Boston answered with 16 straight points, the first 10 from Jayson Tatum, including a seven-point trip: Tatum's four-point play after a flagrant foul on Collin Murray-Boyles, then a Baylor Scheierman three. Tatum had 19 at the half."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "TOR 80, BOS 75",
        "text": "Jordan Walsh's layup with 7:09 left gave Boston its first lead, 66–65, after it had trailed by 22. Tatum didn't score in the quarter, and Toronto closed it on an 8–0 run."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: BOS 98, TOR 93",
        "text": "Tatum's turnaround jumper made it 90–89 with 1:55 left, but RJ Barrett's runner and dunk put Toronto up 93–90 with 1:14 to go. Neemias Queta's dunk cut it to one, Tatum made two free throws for a 94–93 lead with 25.2 seconds left, and Queta and Sam Hauser each made two more, Hauser's after a steal. Toronto scored 13 in the quarter."
      }
    ],
